      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Vertical Increments and the 3% Compounding Rule</h2>
        <p>
          Every executive serving in Levels 6 through 9 is entitled to an annual increment under Fundamental Rule 26. Increments are credited on either <strong>January 1st or July 1st</strong> of each year, based on completing six months of qualifying service:
        </p>
        <div class="callout-box">
          <h4>The Compounding Formula:</h4>
          <p class="formula-box">
            <strong>Next Cell Basic Pay</strong> = Current Cell Pay &plus; ( Current Cell Pay &times; 3% ), rounded off to the nearest hundred rupees.
          </p>
          <p>
            Under the Pay Matrix, employees do not calculate percentages manually. Instead, the salary automatically advances downward to the next vertical cell. For instance, an Inspector in Level 7 moving from Cell 1 (₹1,02,372) to Cell 2 receives ₹1,05,443, gaining an immediate basic pay increase of <strong>₹3,071 per month</strong>, which also lifts their Dearness Allowance and pension contributions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Promotion and MACP Progression: Crossing from Group 'B' to Group 'A'</h2>
        <p>
          The transition from Level 6 to Level 9 involves critical promotional and financial progression under the <strong>Modified Assured Career Progression (MACP)</strong> scheme:
        </p>
        <ol class="editorial-list">
          <li><strong>The 10, 20, 30 Year Milestones:</strong> If an employee spends 10 years in a single post without regular departmental promotion, they are granted financial upgradation to the next functional level (e.g., Level 6 moves to Level 7; Level 7 to Level 8; Level 8 to Level 9; and Level 9 crosses into Group 'A' Level 10).</li>
          <li><strong>Fixation Procedure (Rule 13):</strong> 
            <ul class="sub-list">
              <li><em>Step 1:</em> The employee is granted one notional vertical increment (advancing one cell down in their existing level).</li>
              <li><em>Step 2:</em> The resulting figure is traced into the higher upgraded level. If an identical figure exists, pay is fixed in that cell. If no exact match exists, pay is placed in the <strong>immediate next higher cell</strong> of the new level.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>Non-Functional Upgradation (NFU):</strong> In several central cadres (such as CSS and Audit), officers in Level 8 automatically advance to Level 9 on completion of 4 years of approved regular service, providing a substantial mid-career salary boost without waiting for promotional vacancies.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

